          "title": "You'll want to know: vertragen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vertragen — \"to get along (sich vertragen); to tolerate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Meine Katze und mein Hund vertragen sich gut. My cat and my dog get along well."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Reflexive for to get along: sich vertragen. Without sich it means to tolerate: Ich vertrage keine Milch."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vertragen is inherited from Middle High German vertragen and Old High German fartragan \"to bear, to stand\" (EtymDB), built on tragen \"to carry\", from Proto-Germanic draganą."
            }
          ]
        },
